# Files excluded from the Vercel deployment upload.
#
# Vercel builds two things from this repo: backend/server.js and the CRA app in
# frontend/. Everything listed here is developer- or marketing-facing material
# that neither build reads, so shipping it only inflates the upload.
#
# Every path below is anchored with a leading slash on purpose. The syntax is
# .gitignore's, where a bare "docs/" matches a directory at ANY depth — and the
# CRA app serves two directories that would be caught by exactly that:
#
#   frontend/public/docs/   -> /docs/documentation-index.json, read at runtime
#                              by the help drawer, onboarding tour and assistant
#   frontend/public/assets/ -> /assets/aureoncare-logo.png and the wide logo,
#                              referenced by the login, register and top bar
#
# Excluding either one would build cleanly and then 404 in production, so keep
# these anchored and do not add bare directory names here.

# The repository's own docs tree: written documentation, the demo video harness
# and the rendered marketing videos. The marketing cuts are tens of megabytes
# each; keeping them out of the upload is the reason this file exists.
/docs/

# Deployment tooling for other targets — not used by the Vercel build.
/helm/
/docker/
/deployment/
/update-agent/

# Product collateral committed at the root.
/*.pptx
/*.docx

# Documentation committed at the root: architecture and security material
# (ARCHITECTURE_DIAGRAM, SAST, SSDLC, SEC-05_MULTI_TENANCY_PLAN, audit and
# refactoring guides), operator runbooks (DEPLOYMENT, SETUP, OAUTH_SETUP) and
# business collateral (COMPETITIVE_ANALYSIS, EXECUTIVE_SUMMARY). Between them
# they describe tenancy internals, the security control set and where it is
# still incomplete, and our read of the market — none of which has any reason
# to travel to the deployment.
#
# Neither build reads any of it: the frontend's only prebuild step copies the
# Zoom lib, and nothing in backend/ or frontend/src references a root .md.
# The help drawer's content is a separate tree under frontend/public/docs/
# that this pattern cannot reach.
#
# The pattern is anchored and single-level, so it matches only markdown sitting
# directly at the repo root — backend/**.md and frontend/public/docs/**.md are
# untouched. README.md stays as the repository's front door.
/*.md
!/README.md

# Test and tooling output.
/coverage/
/frontend/coverage/
/playwright-report/
/test-results/
*.log
